  "sourceLocator": {
    "chapter": "Equipment",
    "section": "6.170",
    "heading": "Wearing and Wielding Items",
    "lineStart": 7090,
    "lineEnd": 7094
  },
  "section": "6.170",
  "rulesText": "Using a magic item's properties might mean wearing or wielding it. A magic item meant to be worn must be donned in the intended fashion: boots go on feet, gloves on hands, hats and helmets on a head, and rings on a finger. Magic armor must be donned, a Shield strapped to the arm, a cloak fastened about the shoulders. A weapon must be held.\n\nIn most cases, a magic item that's meant to be worn can fit a creature regardless of size or build. Magic garments are made to be easily adjustable, or they magically adjust themselves to the wearer."
}
